  "details": "Whenever I try and upload anything, I go into the Build Control Panel, get some important messages but nothing that'd prevent me from uploading an avatar, and press the upload button. However, just a second or two later, I get a generic error sound and the process of uploading the avatar doesn't even begin. This is the error I'm getting in Unity's console: https://pastebin.com/imQJPiK9. As a side note, this also prevents me from entering play mode after I try and upload an avatar.\n\nMy version of Unity is 5.6.3p1 Windows 64 bit, and my SDK is up to date.\n\nTo try and fix the issue, I've updated my SDK, uninstalled my SDK, reinstalled my SDK, turned off future proofing, uninstalled/reinstalled Unity, deleted the \"Library, Projectsettings, and Temp\" folders in my Unity project, signed in and out of the VRChat SDK, signed in and out of Unity, and probably other things I'm forgetting at the moment.\n\nNothing thus far has worked, or even gotten close to working.",
